## Version

Pre-1.0. Product SemVer is three parts (`Major.Minor.Patch`). MSIX `Identity Version` is four parts: **`Major.Minor.Patch.0`** — the 4th part (Revision) is **always `0`** (Store requirement). The UI drops Revision.

**Single source of truth:** `<PalaceVersion>` in `Directory.Build.props`. That sets `Version` / `AssemblyVersion` / `FileVersion` / `InformationalVersion` for the solution. After every bump, sync the manifest:

```bash
python3 scripts/sync-appx-version.py
```

CI (`version-check` in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`) fails if props and `Package.appxmanifest` disagree, or if a PR’s version is not **greater than `main`’s** (unless exempt). CI does **not** require a MINOR bump for features — any greater SemVer (usually PATCH) satisfies the gate.

Settings → About (`TxtAppVersion`) and the title-bar subtitle come from `AppVersion`. When you open a new milestone, bump the minor **and** `AppVersion.Milestone` in the same change. About also shows `AppVersion.InfancyNote` (`TxtInfancyNote`): Rooms and Organization are in their infancy — do not claim they are finished.

MSIX identities cannot go backwards. This repo already registered `1.0.1.0` once. **Do not** `winapp unregister` Sacb0y’s release Identity `C20A7629-…` to “fix” a version clash — see `local-test-identity.mdc`; agents use a separate test Identity Name instead.

### Bump rule (every PR that changes the app)

Stay on **0.x** until the first public Store release (**1.0.0**).

| Change | Bump |
|---|---|
| Fixes, polish, small features, library / viewer work | **PATCH** (e.g. `0.2.2` → `0.2.3`) |
| Finished milestone only (explicit Sacb0y open) | **MINOR** (next: Settings restructure → **0.3.0**) |
| Docs / CI / tests only | **No bump** — add label `no-version-bump`, **or** keep the diff on exempt paths (see `scripts/check-version.py`: `.cursor/`, `.github/`, `docs/`, `Palace.Tests/`, `scripts/`, `*.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `ui-tests.ps1`, …) |

Stacked / parallel PRs: rebase onto `main` and **re-bump** in merge order so each tip stays greater than `main`.

Do **not** jump to `1.0.0` because something “feels ready.” Opening a new milestone requires Sacb0y.

### Every bumping PR description must include

1. **New version** (e.g. `0.2.3`)
2. **One-line user-facing summary** (plain wording for Isiac to pass on — changelog is owned elsewhere)

Template fields live in `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`.

| Version | Milestone | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **0.2.x** *(now)* | Library + viewer polish | Details/Info merge, overlay chrome, blur, tags. PATCH freely for library/viewer work. |
| **0.3.0** | Settings restructure | Next **MINOR** — only when that milestone is finished. |
| **bonus** | Cloud | Not a numbered main slice. On-Demand + OAuth already in 0.x; do not download originals. |
| **later 0.x** | Rooms / gamedev / AI | Only when Sacb0y opens them. |
| **1.0.0** | First public Store | Release/trim fixed, Store packaging. |

Leave Revision at `0`. Debug and Release of one commit share the number; the suffix is which binary you launched. Packaged Release is buildable with trim off (`winapp run . --arch x64 -c Release`); re-enable trim only after the ItemsSource COM crash is fixed.
